  61:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_dma.c ****           (+) Configure the DMA interrupt priority using HAL_NVIC_SetPriority()
  62:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_dma.c ****           (+) Enable the DMA IRQ handler using HAL_NVIC_EnableIRQ()
  63:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_dma.c ****           (+) Use HAL_DMA_Start_IT() to start DMA transfer after the configuration of
  64:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_dma.c ****               Source address and destination address and the Length of data to be transferred.
  65:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_dma.c ****               In this case the DMA interrupt is configured
  66:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_dma.c ****           (+) Use HAL_DMA_IRQHandler() called under DMA_IRQHandler() Interrupt subroutine
  67:stm/stm32g4xx/STM32G4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32g4xx_hal_dma.c ****           (+) At the end of data transfer HAL_DMA_IRQHandler() function is executed and user can
